# Enhancement One – Software Engineering

This enhancement focuses on improving the software engineering quality of my original artifact.  
The goal was to strengthen the structure, readability, maintainability, and reliability of the code while applying industry‑standard engineering practices.

---

## 🧩 Original Artifact

My original artifact was the **Weight Tracker Android application**, specifically the classes responsible for:

- Managing user input  
- Updating weight entries  
- Displaying historical data  
- Handling UI logic and navigation  

The code worked, but it had several issues related to structure, clarity, and separation of concerns.

---

## ⚠️ Problems Identified

During the code review and initial analysis, I found several engineering issues:

- UI logic mixed with data logic  
- Repeated code blocks  
- Weak validation for user input  
- Poor separation between Activity and Helper classes  
- Inconsistent naming conventions  
- Lack of comments and documentation  
- Hard‑to‑follow flow between methods  

These issues made the code harder to maintain and more prone to bugs.

---

## 🛠 Enhancement Goals

To improve the software engineering quality, I focused on:

- Refactoring methods for clarity  
- Improving naming conventions  
- Separating UI logic from data logic  
- Adding comments and documentation  
- Reducing repeated code  
- Improving validation and error handling  
- Organizing helper classes more effectively  

These changes make the code easier to understand, maintain, and extend.

---

## 🔧 Enhancements Implemented

Here are the specific improvements I made:

### ✔ Refactored methods  
I reorganized long methods into smaller, more readable functions.

### ✔ Improved naming conventions  
Variables and methods now follow consistent, descriptive naming.

### ✔ Added validation  
User input is now checked before being processed.

### ✔ Improved separation of concerns  
Helper classes handle data logic, while Activities handle UI logic.

### ✔ Added comments  
Key sections of the code now include clear explanations.

### ✔ Removed repeated code  
Shared logic was moved into reusable helper methods.

---

## 📈 Impact of the Enhancement

These improvements resulted in:

- Cleaner and more readable code  
- Better maintainability  
- Reduced risk of bugs  
- More professional structure  
- Easier future enhancements  
- Stronger alignment with software engineering best practices  

This enhancement demonstrates my ability to apply engineering principles to real code and improve its quality significantly.

---

## 📝 Reflection

Enhancing this artifact taught me the importance of structure and clarity in software engineering.  
By refactoring and reorganizing the code, I improved both functionality and maintainability.  
This enhancement shows my growth in applying engineering principles and producing professional‑quality code.

